from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;a=json.loads((r/'analysis/comparison.json').read_text());audit=json.loads((r/'input_audit.json').read_text());timing=json.loads((r/'source_timing.json').read_text());result=a['replay_result'];h=a['health'];checks=a['distance_and_return_checks'];overall=a['overall_return_check'];source=Path(audit['source_bag']);sha=hashlib.sha256()
with source.open('rb') as f:
 for block in iter(lambda:f.read(8*1024*1024),b''):sha.update(block)
(r/'source.sha256').write_text(sha.hexdigest()+'  '+str(source)+'\n')
lines=['# Classic bag odometry comparison','',f"Source: `{source}`. Duration {audit['duration_s']:.3f} s; {audit['messages']:,} recorded messages.",'','Route supplied by the operator: 3 m forward, wait, 3 m back, wait; then 5 m forward, wait, 5 m back, wait.','', '| Check | Point-LIO | Vendor odometry |','|---|---:|---:|']
for c in checks:
 target=c['nominal_distance_m'];l,v=c['point_lio'],c['vendor']
 lines += [f"| {target:g} m outbound horizontal displacement | {l['outbound_horizontal_endpoint_distance_m']:.4f} m | {v['outbound_horizontal_endpoint_distance_m']:.4f} m |",f"| {target:g} m inbound horizontal displacement | {l['inbound_horizontal_endpoint_distance_m']:.4f} m | {v['inbound_horizontal_endpoint_distance_m']:.4f} m |",f"| {target:g} m leg return offset | {100*l['return_horizontal_offset_m']:.2f} cm | {100*v['return_horizontal_offset_m']:.2f} cm |"]
lines += [f"| Final horizontal offset from original start | {100*overall['point_lio']['final_horizontal_offset_from_original_start_m']:.2f} cm | {100*overall['vendor']['final_horizontal_offset_from_original_start_m']:.2f} cm |",f"| Final height change from original start | {100*overall['point_lio']['final_vertical_offset_from_original_start_m']:.2f} cm | {100*overall['vendor']['final_vertical_offset_from_original_start_m']:.2f} cm |",'','![Comparison plot](analysis/comparison.png)','','## Integrity and replay','',f"All {audit['chunks']:,} zstd chunks decompress; full container traversal and metadata message counts agree. The summary CRC is present and matches. Data chunks have no recorded CRC, so this is not a per-payload CRC guarantee. Every mapping input was deserialized; this check does not claim that every other topic uses a correct advertised schema.",'',f"Saved raw/body conversion checked against {audit['geometry_matches']:,} matching points across {audit['geometry_pairs']} scans; maximum residual {audit['geometry_max_residual_m']*1e6:.3f} micrometres. This confirms the recorded topic conversion, not an independent mount survey.",'',f"The source contains no Point-LIO output, so Point-LIO was recomputed using the existing binary, body IMU bias calibration, approved extrinsics and zero time-lag setting. A temporary startup override sets init_map_size=4000, as in the successful previous 3 m/5 m test. Application code/configuration hashes before and after agree: **{result['application_unchanged']}**.",'',f"Separate Humble-compatible SQLite replay was prepared because this bag has Jetson Jazzy metadata. Source MCAP was opened read-only and is SHA-256 identified in source.sha256. Isolated DDS domain 209, localhost only, 0.5x playback; only sensor/odometry/clock/TF topics published. No robot command topics replayed.",'',f"Cloud delivery matched all {result['input_cloud_messages']:,} source stamps exactly: **{result['cloud_delivery_exact']}**. Calibrated body IMU delivery matched all {result['input_imu_messages']:,} output stamps exactly: **{result['imu_delivery_exact']}**. Identical duplicate SportModeState samples dropped: {audit['calibrated_imu_duplicates_dropped']}; converter errors: {audit['body_converter_errors']}.",'',f"Replay stop reason: `{result['stop_reason']}`. {h['lio_poses']:,} poses, mean {h['average_pose_frequency_hz']:.3f} Hz. Pose timestamps nonincreasing: {h['nonincreasing_pose_stamps']}; nonfinite pose values: {h['nonfinite_pose_values']}; translation steps >15 cm: {h['steps_over_0_15_m']}; rotation steps >5 degrees: {h['rotation_steps_over_5_deg']}. Maximum single step {h['lio_step_translation_m']['max']:.4f} m, {h['lio_step_rotation_deg']['max']:.3f} degrees.",'',f"Global TF parent conflicts: {result['multiple_tf_parents']}. Missing map->odom stamps: {h['tf_missing_pose_stamp_count']}; extra stamps: {h['tf_extra_stamp_count']}. Exact full pose/TF stamp sequence match: {h['tf_pose_stamps_exact']}. Deferred TF lookup retries in logs can occur before the exact-time vendor transform arrives; they do not by themselves mean a pose was dropped.",'','## Timing','',f"Raw clouds have no duplicate or backward header stamps and no gaps over three median scan periods; median period {timing['raw']['positive_dt_median_p95_p99_max_s'][0]*1000:.3f} ms. Body IMU has no backward stamps after duplicate filtering; {timing['imu']['source_gaps_over_3_median_count']} gaps exceed three median periods, maximum {timing['imu']['positive_dt_median_p95_p99_max_s'][-1]*1000:.3f} ms. Source gaps are retained, not interpolated or hidden. Detailed nearby Point-LIO steps are in comparison.json.",'',f"{timing['scans_imu_bracketed']['within_recording']} / {sum(timing['scans_imu_bracketed'][k] for k in ['within_recording','outside_recording'])} scans lie within the IMU recording boundaries; only the first scan begins before the first IMU sample. Point-LIO starts at {h['first_pose_s']:.3f} s, after that boundary.",'','Recorder receipt minus robot header time includes an approximately 25.7 s clock offset. It must not be interpreted as 25.7 s network latency without independent clock synchronization. Source header times were preserved; no host/robot offset or acquisition-lag value was fitted to make the result look better. Zero acquisition lag is still uncalibrated. This replay does not establish exact LiDAR/IMU acquisition synchronization.','','## Hold selection and floor consistency','','Seconds below refer to the first raw-cloud header stamp. Medians use quiet interiors of the recorded waits, selected from vendor motion; there is no per-leg trajectory alignment or scale fit. Vendor positions are converted from base_link to the IMU using the developer URDF lever arm. Plot paths use one initial heading/translation for each estimate, preserving gravity axes.','']
for name,hold in a['holds'].items():lines += [f"- {name}: {hold['time_window_s'][0]:g}–{hold['time_window_s'][1]:g} s; Point-LIO position p95 radius {hold['lio_position_p95_distance_to_median_m']*100:.3f} cm, body gyro RMS {hold['body_gyro_rms_rad_s']:.4f} rad/s."]
lines += ['','Repeated floor heights use the same map XY cells directly, with no ICP or levelling. Candidate floor: within 3 m of initial IMU, 0.15–0.9 m below it, 15 cm cells containing at least 5 points.']
for f in a['revisited_start_floor_checks']:
 if f['common_15cm_xy_cells']:lines += [f"- {f['hold']}: {f['common_15cm_xy_cells']} common cells; median absolute difference {1000*f['median_absolute_floor_height_difference_m']:.2f} mm; p90 {1000*f['p90_absolute_floor_height_difference_m']:.2f} mm."]
lines += ['','The only missing map->odom transform is the final output pose, 19.36 ms beyond the last derived vendor TF at the recording boundary. Every earlier pose matches the TF stamp sequence exactly; this does not affect any selected endpoint hold.','','Point-LIO estimates the 3 m far hold 6.61 cm below its start and the 5 m far hold 11.01 cm below its own start, then returns close to the original height. This could include actual slope or gravity/map tilt; the bag alone cannot distinguish them. The small return-height residual and floor-repeat medians are not proof of absolute vertical accuracy. Quiet-hold position p95 radii are about 1.5–3.0 cm, so do not interpret the 1.97 cm final median offset as a precise 2 cm absolute accuracy guarantee.']
lines += ['','## Measurement limits','']+['- '+s for s in a['measurement_limitations']]+['','Detailed numbers: [comparison.json](analysis/comparison.json). Input audits: [input_audit.json](input_audit.json), [source_timing.json](source_timing.json). Replay completion/delivery: [result.json](result.json).']
(r/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print(r/'REPORT.md')
